WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.755 --> 00:00:14.816
was a quiet morning in the mountains near Metro City.

2
00:00:16.076 --> 00:00:19.137
Kaboom! An explosion sent dirt and rocks flying.

3
00:00:20.557 --> 00:00:23.698
When the dust settled, a construction worker peeked out from behind a boulder.

4
00:00:23.718 --> 00:00:25.639
"All clear!"

5
00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:26.519
she yelled.

6
00:00:26.539 --> 00:00:29.160
"All clear!"

7
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:30.580
other workers yelled.

8
00:00:31.828 --> 00:00:34.250
More workers came out from behind trees and boulders.

9
00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.511
They carried shovels and pickaxes.

10
00:00:38.213 --> 00:00:40.654
The workers were building a new road on the side of a mountain.

11
00:00:42.676 --> 00:00:44.237
Everyone approached the blast area.

12
00:00:44.737 --> 00:00:47.239
It was now a flat surface littered with broken rocks.

13
00:00:47.859 --> 00:00:49.560
A rock wall rose above the area.

14
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:53.283
"Let's move these rocks out of the way," the woman said.

15
00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:54.964
"You got it, Beth!"

16
00:00:55.524 --> 00:00:57.026
A worker climbed into a bulldozer.

17
00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:03.120
Brumm! Brumm!

18
00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:04.841
Another worker stared at the rock wall.

19
00:01:05.502 --> 00:01:06.603
There were holes in the rock.

20
00:01:07.103 --> 00:01:08.504
Something sparkled from within.

21
00:01:08.524 --> 00:01:12.547
"Something's behind that rock wall," he said.

22
00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:14.088
"It looks like metal."

23
00:01:14.728 --> 00:01:16.189
"Stop the bulldozer!"

24
00:01:18.331 --> 00:01:19.452
Beth took a closer look.

25
00:01:19.472 --> 00:01:21.213
"You're right, Phil.

26
00:01:21.633 --> 00:01:22.594
Let's see what it is."

27
00:01:24.355 --> 00:01:26.737
Pickaxes swung as the workers chipped away at the rock.

28
00:01:29.038 --> 00:01:31.080
Soon a huge bronze door was revealed.

29
00:01:32.748 --> 00:01:33.368
Phil whistled.

30
00:01:33.388 --> 00:01:36.310
"It's big enough for a giant!"

31
00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:38.731
"I wonder who made it," Beth said.

32
00:01:39.311 --> 00:01:40.271
Phil stepped closer.

33
00:01:40.291 --> 00:01:43.112
"And what's on the other side?"

34
00:01:43.532 --> 00:01:44.053
He knocked.

35
00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:48.314
"Ouch!" Phil shook his hand and then rubbed his knuckles.

36
00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.915
"That door must be really thick!"

37
00:01:50.936 --> 00:01:54.437
"Well, there's no answer," another worker said.

38
00:01:54.457 --> 00:01:56.578
"I guess no one's—" Rumble!

39
00:01:56.958 --> 00:01:59.179
Rumble! The mountain shook!

40
00:01:59.779 --> 00:02:00.800
Phil lost his balance.

41
00:02:03.424 --> 00:02:05.405
"Oof!" Then Roar!

42
00:02:06.066 --> 00:02:07.426
The huge door rattled!

43
00:02:07.967 --> 00:02:09.227
Dust fell from its hinges.

44
00:02:09.928 --> 00:02:10.568
Beth gulped.

45
00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:13.590
"Someone is home!

46
00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:18.533
Run!" "Okay, Roxy," Mara said.

47
00:02:18.553 --> 00:02:21.714
"What would you buy if you had a million dollars?"

48
00:02:23.996 --> 00:02:26.017
It was morning at Metro City Elementary School.

49
00:02:26.757 --> 00:02:29.639
Roxy and her friends were playing basketball before school started.

50
00:02:29.659 --> 00:02:31.300
"I don't know."

51
00:02:33.172 --> 00:02:34.473
Roxy took a shot and missed.

52
00:02:34.493 --> 00:02:38.335
"Maybe I'd buy a swimming pool."

53
00:02:39.115 --> 00:02:40.416
The ball bounced to Terrell.

54
00:02:40.436 --> 00:02:44.578
"You don't need a million dollars to buy a swimming pool," he said.

55
00:02:45.518 --> 00:02:47.479
He tried to take a shot, but Jack blocked him.

56
00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.000
Terrell passed the ball to Mara.

57
00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:54.082
"I wish you did have a pool, Roxy," Jack said.

58
00:02:54.102 --> 00:02:56.924
"I'd live at your house—just like Terrell."

59
00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:01.261
"Terrell's only staying with Roxy for two weeks, Jack."

60
00:03:01.542 --> 00:03:02.962
Mara dribbled past Roxy.

61
00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.263
"He doesn't live there."

62
00:03:06.304 --> 00:03:07.684
Jack stole the ball from Mara.

63
00:03:07.704 --> 00:03:10.485
"Hey!" Mara frowned.

64
00:03:10.986 --> 00:03:13.147
"What would you do with a million dollars, Jack?"

65
00:03:13.547 --> 00:03:14.227
Roxy asked.

66
00:03:15.127 --> 00:03:16.488
Jack took a shot and scored.

67
00:03:16.508 --> 00:03:19.549
"I'd buy a Jet Ski."

68
00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:21.630
Terrell rolled his eyes.

69
00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:25.212
"You don't need a million dollars to buy a Jet Ski either."

70
00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.642
"You do if it's a flying Jet Ski," Jack said.

71
00:03:30.742 --> 00:03:31.482
Everyone laughed.

72
00:03:33.863 --> 00:03:35.144
Then Roxy's watch beeped.

73
00:03:35.864 --> 00:03:36.905
She glanced at her friends.

74
00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:38.785
"I'll be right back.

75
00:03:39.326 --> 00:03:40.686
I'm thirsty."

76
00:03:42.447 --> 00:03:44.048
She stepped away and opened her watch.

77
00:03:44.068 --> 00:03:46.429
"Hey, Mayor," Roxy said.

78
00:03:46.449 --> 00:03:48.109
"Is everything okay?"

79
00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.311
"We might have a problem," Mayor Bloom said.

80
00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:54.052
"Workers are building a new road in the mountains.

81
00:03:54.616 --> 00:03:57.458
They blasted some rock and discovered something strange."

82
00:03:57.478 --> 00:03:58.959
"What is it?"

83
00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.220
Roxy asked.

84
00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.303
"It's a big door," the mayor said.

85
00:04:04.604 --> 00:04:05.704
Roxy scratched her head.

86
00:04:05.724 --> 00:04:07.166
"Did they open it?"

87
00:04:07.186 --> 00:04:09.567
"No," Mayor Bloom said.

88
00:04:09.587 --> 00:04:11.509
"But something is behind it.

89
00:04:11.969 --> 00:04:15.132
Whatever it is, it made the whole mountain shake!"

90
00:04:15.152 --> 00:04:18.754
"Don't worry, Mayor," Roxy said.

91
00:04:18.774 --> 00:04:20.656
"I'm on my way!"
